    "hero": {
      "type": "cls-neera-hero",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Afternoon Slump? 10 Reasons to Rethink Your Water Bottle",
        "subhead": "There is one object you drink from all day and almost never think about. When the afternoons drag, the stomach is unsettled and you feel older than your years, it is the last thing you would suspect. Here are ten reasons to give it a second look.",
        "avatar_image_fallback": "neera-favicon-180.png",
        "byline_details": "By the Neera Living team\n\nUpdated November 2026\nLab-Tested Pure Copper Collection"
      }
    },
    "problem": {
      "type": "cls-neera-problem",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "The one thing we never question",
        "paragraph_1": "<p>When the afternoons get heavy and the body feels a little older, we look at sleep, at food and at the calendar. Almost nobody looks at <strong>the bottle they drink from every day</strong>, year after year.</p>",
        "paragraph_2": "<p>It is worth a look. <strong>Plastic bottles</strong> shed tiny particles into the water they hold, more so with heat and reuse. <strong>Aluminum bottles</strong> rely on an inner coating you never see. <strong>Steel</strong> is sturdy, but it is only a container. <strong>Copper is different.</strong> Families in India have kept their drinking water in copper for centuries, and the metal itself behaves differently from the rest.</p>",
        "paragraph_3": "<p>We are not promising that one bottle changes how you feel. This is an invitation to take one constant source of plastic out of your day and put a <strong>solid copper vessel</strong> in its place.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-problem-materials.jpg"
      }
    },
