    "reason-10": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "10",
        "heading": "One source of microplastics you can simply stop adding.",
        "body": "<p>Plastic bottles shed <strong>tiny plastic particles</strong> into the water they hold, and researchers now find those particles in people. Nobody can yet say what a lifetime of them does. What you can decide is how many more you add. Water kept in a <strong>solid copper bottle</strong> touches copper, not plastic. You are not doing a dramatic <strong>“detox.”</strong> You are simply closing one tap.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-10.jpg",
        "image_position": "left",
        "background": "cream"
      }
    },
    "reason-9": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "9",
        "heading": "Plastic and even some metals are not neutral.",
        "body": "<p>Every bottle puts something against your water. In <strong>plastic</strong>, it is plastic, and its compounds move into the water faster in a hot car or after months of refills. In most <strong>aluminum</strong> bottles, it is a thin inner coating rather than the metal you see. <strong>Steel</strong> is the stable one, yet it adds nothing and does nothing. <strong>Bare copper</strong> is the exception: nothing is coated onto it, and its surface is naturally hard on microbes, a property documented for more than a century. The difference is in the material itself.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-9-materials.jpg",
        "image_position": "right",
        "background": "cream-alt"
      }
    },
    "reason-8": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "8",
        "heading": "Copper has been used for water storage for centuries.",
        "body": "<p><strong>Tamra Jal </strong>— water stored in copper — is not a social-media invention. Families across the Indian subcontinent have kept water in copper vessels for generations. The practice is part of a broader understanding that the vessel matters as much as the water itself. <strong>Neera</strong> simply brings that <strong>tradition into a modern,</strong> leak-proof, hand-hammered form that fits real life: car cup holders, travel, and daily desks.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-8.jpg",
        "image_position": "left",
        "background": "cream"
      }
    },
    "reason-7": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "7",
        "heading": "A naturally antimicrobial surface.",
        "body": "<p><strong>Bare copper</strong> is hard on microbes, and that is measured, not folklore. In a 2012 lab study, water deliberately contaminated with bacteria such as E. coli and kept in copper pots at room temperature had <strong>no recoverable bacteria after 16 hours</strong> (Sudha et al., J Health Popul Nutr). In a Neera bottle the water rests against that same kind of surface, with no lining in between. Plastic and steel simply hold your water. <strong>This comes from the metal itself, not from a slogan</strong>, and it is still no substitute for starting with water that is safe to drink.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-7.jpg",
        "image_position": "right",
        "background": "cream-alt"
      }
    },
    "reason-6": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "6",
        "heading": "It turns hydration into a ritual.",
        "body": "<p>It asks for very little: pour the water in before bed and it is <strong>ready when you wake.</strong> That simple sequence transforms something automatic into something intentional. Many <strong>Neera </strong>owners tell us the ritual itself <strong>changes</strong> how they <strong>relate to water.</strong> It is no longer just another bottle on the desk - it is a <strong>quiet daily practice.</strong></p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-6.jpg",
        "image_position": "left",
        "background": "cream"
      }
    },
    "reason-5": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "5",
        "heading": "Hand-hammered means more contact area.",
        "body": "<p>A smooth, machine-made <strong>copper</strong> bottle looks fine. A hammered one works harder. Every dimple leaves a little more copper against the <strong>water</strong>, and working the metal by hand hardens it, so the thin wall shrugs off small knocks and the texture sits securely in your hand. Artisans in India hammer each Neera bottle by hand. <strong>No two are identical</strong>, and that is exactly the idea.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-5.jpg",
        "image_position": "right",
        "background": "cream-alt"
      }
    },
    "reason-4": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "4",
        "heading": "Lab-tested purity you can verify.",
        "body": "<p>Not every bottle sold as copper is solid copper. Some are steel or <strong>aluminum</strong> under a thin copper layer, and some mix in other metals. An independent <strong>lab analysis</strong> of the Neera bottle measured over 99.9% copper, and the Essentials Set comes with access to the Certificate of Authenticity, so you can read the result yourself. Two quick checks at home: <strong>a magnet does not grip solid copper</strong>, and the bare inside darkens within a week or two of daily use. Simple checks, and they are the ones that matter.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-4.jpg",
        "image_position": "left",
        "background": "cream"
      }
    },
    "reason-3": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "3",
        "heading": "Designed for real life, not just the shelf.",
        "body": "<p>34 ounces — enough for a full day of <strong>intentional sipping</strong>. Leak-proof threaded cap that opens and closes with a single twist. Dimensions that fit most standard U.S. car cup holders and kitchen cabinets. Weight that feels solid without being heavy. Every bottle ships with a <strong>Copper Care Brush</strong> and a Travel Sleeve. This is not a decorative object. It is built to be used every day.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-3.jpg",
        "image_position": "right",
        "background": "cream-alt"
      }
    },
    "reason-2": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "2",
        "heading": "Better for the planet — and for the bottles that come after yours.",
        "body": "<p>One<strong> copper bottle</strong> replaces hundreds of single-use plastic bottles over its lifetime. <strong>Pure copper </strong>does not degrade the way plastic does. With simple care it can serve for <strong>decades </strong>and, i<strong>n many families, </strong>become something that is passed on. Choosing <strong>Neera </strong>is not another purchase in a <strong>cycle</strong> of replacements. It is a decision to step out of that cycle.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-2.jpg",
        "image_position": "left",
        "background": "cream"
      }
    },
    "reason-1": {
      "type": "cls-neera-reason",
      "settings": {
        "number": "1",
        "heading": "The Neera promise: a small brand that takes every order seriously.",
        "body": "<p>We are not a giant corporation. We are a small team that built <strong>Neera </strong>around one idea: everyday drinkware <strong>should be made with natural materials,</strong> real craftsmanship, and integrity. If something is not right with your order, reach out. <strong>We will make it right</strong> — no run-around, no script. Free shipping on every order. Use code <strong>NEERA10</strong> for an extra <strong>10% </strong>off. Buy more and save up to 15%. You are not only buying a bottle. You are supporting a way of making things that still cares about the person on the other end.</p>",
        "photo_image_fallback": "neera-reason-1.jpg",
        "image_position": "right",
        "background": "cream-alt"
      }
    },
